WC-BUG-002 — Cart May Allow Quantity Above Available Stock

Module: Product Inventory / Shopping Cart

Severity: Medium (provisional; subject to business rules)

Priority:high

Status: Suspected — verification required

Environment: WholeCart browser-based test environment

Product: Chef's Banana Chips


Preconditions

Buyer is logged in.

Chef's Banana Chips is available in the product listing.

The product listing displays stock availability of 1 piece.

Steps to Reproduce

Open the Chef's Banana Chips product listing.

Record the displayed available stock and unit price.

Add the product to the cart.

Inspect the cart quantity and line-item amount.

Check whether the quantity can be increased beyond the displayed stock.

Observe whether the application displays a validation message or prevents an invalid quantity.

Expected Result

The cart should not allow a buyer to purchase more units than the available stock, unless the displayed stock has a different documented meaning.

Invalid quantities should be rejected with a clear validation message.

Inventory availability should be validated before order placement.

Actual Result

Observed:

Product listing displays available stock of 1 piece.

Unit price is ₹365.00 per piece.

Requires verification:

The cart amount appears to be ₹3,650.00, which would correspond to 10 pieces at ₹365.00 each.

The actual cart quantity has not yet been confirmed.

It has not been confirmed whether the application permits checkout with a quantity exceeding available stock.

Business Impact

If the cart permits purchases beyond actual inventory availability, buyers may place orders that cannot be fulfilled, leading to order cancellations, inventory inconsistencies, or customer dissatisfaction.

